CON-06: scale snow plowed to another subcatchment by both subcatchments' areas

snow_plowSnow() added sfrac[4] * exc * fArea_j / fArea_m to the depth of the
receiving subcatchment's pervious pack. The fArea are fractions of each
subcatchment's own area, so the plowed volume was multiplied by A_m / A_j
whenever the two subcatchments differ in size. Multiply each fraction by its
subcatchment's non-LID area, as the "plow out of system" branch and
snow_getSnowCover() do, so the volume is conserved.

Apply from the root of a Stormwater-Management-Model checkout at cb3e192b:
    git apply CON-06_swmm530.patch

diff --git a/src/legacy/engine/snow.c b/src/legacy/engine/snow.c
index d415675..3afc00a 100644
--- a/src/legacy/engine/snow.c
+++ b/src/legacy/engine/snow.c
@@ -478,12 +478,16 @@ void snow_plowSnow(int subcatchIndex, double tStep)
                 m = Snowmelt[k].toSubcatch;
                 if ( Subcatch[m].snowpack )
                 {
-                    f = Subcatch[m].snowpack->fArea[SNOW_PERV];
+                    f = Subcatch[m].snowpack->fArea[SNOW_PERV] *
+                        (Subcatch[m].area - Subcatch[m].lidArea);
                 } 
                 else f = 0.0; 
                 if ( f > 0.0 )
                 {
-                    f = snowpack->fArea[SNOW_PLOWABLE] / f;
+                    // --- ratio of plowable area to receiving pervious area
+                    f = snowpack->fArea[SNOW_PLOWABLE] *
+                        (Subcatch[subcatchIndex].area -
+                         Subcatch[subcatchIndex].lidArea) / f;
                     Subcatch[m].snowpack->wsnow[SNOW_PERV] +=
                         Snowmelt[k].sfrac[4] * exc * f;
                     sfracTotal += Snowmelt[k].sfrac[4];
